OVERVIEW:

 This program reads magic squares from files in a particular
 format and determines their validity as a magic square. It
 can also write magic squares in this same format using an
 algorithm which uses a given odd-number dimension and file
 path to write the square to.


INCLUDED FILES:

 * MagicSquare.java - mandatory class file
 * MagicSquareDriver.java - mandatory driver file
 * MagicSquareInterface.java - mandatory interface file for MagicSquare class
 * README - this file


COMPILING AND RUNNING:

 There are no subdirectories present nor needed for this
 program to run. Only this program's driver class needs to
 be compiled; all other source files will be compiled
 automatically. In order to compile it successfully, the
 command-line's working directory should be the same as
 the program's directory, then execute the following command:
 $ javac MagicSquareDriver.java

 In order for the program to exit successfully, it first
 needs a valid combination of arguments for validating and
 generating squares. In order to validate squares, execute
 the command
 $ java MagicSquareDriver -check <filename>
 ... where filename is a valid file path with a correctly
 formatted pre-existing magic square. In order to generate
 squares, execute the command
 $ java MagicSquareDriver -create <filename> <size>
 ... where filename is the desired write path, which is not
 required to exist prior to execution, and size is an odd
 integer that is at least three which is necessary for the
 algorithm to generate squares.

 The console which the program is executed in will print the
 results of both validating and generating squares.


